          "python",
          "Good context for \"What is model overfitting?\":\n\"Overfitting occurs when a model learns to fit training data too closely, including \nnoise and random variations. Overfitted models perform well on training data but \npoorly on new, unseen data. Regularization and cross-validation help prevent overfitting.\"\n\nPoor context (but might be retrieved if using simple keyword matching):\n\"The model was fitted to the data using maximum likelihood estimation. Fitting took \n12 hours on our GPU cluster. We fit the model parameters using Adam optimizer.\""
        ]
      ]
